  "result": "Perfect! The bulk discount feature is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation\n\n**Added to `src/totals.js`:**\n- `lineBulkDiscount()` - Private helper function that calculates 2.5% discount for lines with 10+ units\n- Updated `lineVAT()` - Now applies bulk discount after line discount, before VAT calculation\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` - Includes bulk discount in the total discount field\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Lines with qty \u2265 10 automatically get an additional 2.5% discount\n2. This bulk discount is applied **after** the line's own discount (or tier discount)\n3. VAT is calculated on the amount remaining after both discounts\n4. The bulk discount is included in `invoiceTotals.discount` field\n\n**Example calculation** (line with 10 units):\n- lineTotal: 10 \u00d7 1000 = 10,000\n- lineDiscount (5% tier): 10,000 \u00d7 5% = 500\n- bulkDiscount (2.5% of remainder): 9,500 \u00d7 2.5% = 238\n- amountAfterBothDiscounts: 10,000 - 500 - 238 = 9,262\n- VAT (21%): 9,262 \u00d7 21% = 1,945\n- total: 9,262 + 1,945 = 11,207\n\n**Tests added:**\n- 13 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Bulk discount at exactly 10 units\n  - No bulk discount below 10 units\n  - Interaction with line discounts\n  - Interaction with VAT\n  - Interaction with tier discounts\n  - Interaction with multiple lines\n  - Interaction with vouchers\n  - Edge cases and boundary testing\n\n**Results:** \u2705 All 401 tests pass (388 existing + 13 new bulk discount tests)",
